# Wave D.c — Manifest-driven operator shell chrome

## Problem

Hostile audit blocker #4: hard-coded `pluginId` branches in the admin shell.

| File | Branch | Effect |
| ---- | ------ | ------ |
| `apps/web/src/shell/tours-wizard-layout.tsx` | `pluginId === DENALI_PLUGIN_ID` | Wizard Bridge vs Phase 3 AppShell |
| `apps/web/src/shell/app-shell.tsx` | `pluginId === "urban"` | Extra Catalog + Urban settings nav links |

Those literals block drop-in workspaces and contradict “manifest as SoT”.

## Decision

### 1. Tours wizard layout → extended-create Set

Denali already declares `wizardCreate.extendedChrome: true`, which codegen emits as `WORKSPACE_WIZARD_EXTENDED_CREATE_PLUGIN_IDS` (consumed by `WizardBridgeShell` and `isExtendedOperatorWorkspace`).

`ToursWizardLayout` selects Wizard Bridge when the operator session is present **and** `isExtendedOperatorWorkspace(pluginId)` — no Denali id import.

### 2. Phase 3 AppShell nav → `operatorShell.phase3NavLinks`

Urban (and any future workspace) declares optional Phase 3 header links in `workspace.manifest.json`:

```json
"operatorShell": {
  "phase3NavLinks": [
    { "href": "/catalog", "labelKey": "catalog" },
    { "href": "/settings/workspace-owner", "labelKey": "workspaceOwnerSettings" }
  ]
}
```

`labelKey` resolves under the existing `tours.shell` next-intl namespace (stable message keys; product copy can stay branded).

Codegen emits `apps/web/src/bootstrap/operator-shell-nav-bindings.generated.ts`:

- `WORKSPACE_OPERATOR_SHELL_NAV` — pluginId → frozen link list
- `resolveOperatorShellNavLinks(pluginId)` — empty array when unset

`AppShell` maps that list; zero product id literals.

## Out of scope

- ~~Renaming `urbanSettings` i18n key / `/settings/urban` route~~ → Wave H.i.b `/settings/workspace-owner`
- Hard-coded API `workspaceType === "denali"` commerce branches
- WizardBridge tagline uses `extendedCreateChromeTagline` when extended chrome is on (Gap Closure B.15; was `denaliTagline`)

## Verify

```bash
pnpm run generate:workspace-registry
pnpm run guard:workspace-registry-fresh
rg 'DENALI_PLUGIN_ID|URBAN_WORKSPACE_PLUGIN_ID|=== \"urban\"|=== \"denali\"' \
  apps/web/src/shell/app-shell.tsx apps/web/src/shell/tours-wizard-layout.tsx
pnpm --filter @apps/web exec node --import tsx --test test/operator-shell-nav.spec.ts
```
